cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this poster, please cite it as below."
title: "Is the DataSquad Model For You? (US-RSE '26 poster)"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Poster for the US Research Software Engineer Association 2026 conference
  (US-RSE '26, San Jose). It describes the DataSquad model, in which paid
  undergraduate analysts support researchers with data and learn the work by
  doing it, using examples from the Carleton College and UCLA programs. This
  repository holds the poster source (Quarto and Typst), not the alumni data. AI assistance: Claude (Anthropic) helped write the layout
  code and some wording, and Gemini Notebook generated the drawings the icons
  were traced from; the authors reviewed the output and are responsible for it.
